{
  "_comment": "Canonical source of truth for reserved hotkey shortcuts and the hotkey key vocabulary. The backend reads this file directly; a byte-identical copy lives at voice_typer/client/src/renderer/src/data/hotkey_reserved.json because importing via the @server alias resolved outside the renderer root and crashed Vite's dev server during HMR on locale switch. Drift is caught by tests/test_hotkey_reserved_sync.py and the pre-commit hook (id: hotkey-reserved-sync).",
  "_format": {
    "universal_reserved": "Array of hotkey strings blocked on EVERY platform. Stored lowercase with angle brackets, e.g. \"<alt>+<tab>\". Entries are compared after canonicalization, so <win>, <super> and <cmd> all match.",
    "per_platform_reserved": "Object mapping platform key (win32/darwin/linux) to array of hotkey strings blocked on that platform only. win32 also carries Ctrl+Alt+Delete (both spellings), the secure-attention sequence low-level hooks never see.",
    "blocked_ctrl_letters": "Array of single lowercase letters blocked when the hotkey is PURE Ctrl+<letter> (no other modifier). Covers Copy/Paste/Undo/Save/Select All/etc.",
    "modifiers": "Array of modifier key names AND their alias spellings recognized in hotkey strings (pynput-style, lowercase). hotkey_spec.MODIFIER_ALIASES is derived from this list: the renderer and backend must classify a raw token the same way, so a missing alias makes the two count a combo's keys differently.",
    "key_aliases": "Object mapping non-canonical non-modifier key spellings to their canonical token. Applied by the shared parser (hotkey_spec.parse_hotkey and the renderer's normalizeKeyToken) before matching, duplicate detection, or display.",
    "keys": "Object mapping every canonical non-modifier key token to {wire, platforms}. wire is the name the native listeners emit; platforms lists where the token is deliverable. A token absent from keys is unknown_key; a token whose platforms excludes the current platform is key_not_delivered. Modifier tokens are not listed here (see modifiers)."
  },
  "universal_reserved": [
    "<esc>",
    "<alt>+<tab>",
    "<alt>+<f4>",
    "<alt>+<esc>",
    "<alt>+<space>",
    "<enter>",
    "<ctrl>+<enter>",
